{"metadata":{"title":"SuffixAutomaton","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SuffixAutomaton"}],"externalID":"s:16SuffixStructures0A9AutomatonV","symbolKind":"struct","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/GrafluentCollections\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton.swift#L24","fileName":"SuffixAutomaton.swift"},"roleHeading":"Structure","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SuffixAutomaton","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"SuffixStructures"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The suffix automaton of a text: the smallest deterministic automaton that accepts every suffix"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of it, whose paths from the start state spell exactly the text’s substrings (Blumer et al.,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"“The Smallest Automaton Recognizing the Subwords of a Text”, 1985)."}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SuffixAutomaton"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable"}]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is built one symbol at a time in O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":") expected steps, with at most 2"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" − 1 states and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"3"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" − 4 transitions. Each state stands for the substrings that end at the same set of places"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in the text; its suffix link leads to the state of the longest of their suffixes that ends at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"more places. A pattern is checked in O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"m","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":") transitions."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let automaton = SuffixAutomaton(\"abcbc\")","automaton.contains(\"cbc\")              \/\/ true","automaton.occurrenceCount(of: \"bc\")    \/\/ 2","automaton.firstOccurrence(of: \"cb\")    \/\/ 2 ..< 4","automaton.distinctSubstringCount       \/\/ 12","automaton.longestCommonSubstring(with: \"xbcbz\")?.textRange  \/\/ 1 ..< 4, \"bcb\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Transitions from a state come in the order of their symbols: sorted when ","type":"text"},{"code":"Symbol","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Comparable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", otherwise in the order the symbols first occur in the text. The automaton is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"directed graph, ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton\/transitionsView-swift.property","type":"reference"},{"text":", and its suffix links are a tree that converts to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Grafluent’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Arborescence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"code":"Arborescence(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/suffixstructures\/suffixautomaton"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton\/CommonSubstring","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton\/TransitionsView-swift.struct"],"title":"Structures","anchor":"Structures","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton\/init(_:)"],"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton\/count","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton\/distinctSubstringCount","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton\/stateCount","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton\/transitionCount","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton\/transitionsView-swift.property"],"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton\/contains(_:)","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton\/firstOccurrence(of:)","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton\/hasSuffix(_:)","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton\/longestCommonSubstring(with:)","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton\/occurrenceCount(of:)"],"ti